WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:07.270
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:07.270 --> 00:00:11.750
I think the purpose of learning is-- it's just

00:00:11.750 --> 00:00:14.140
aligned with the purpose of living.

00:00:14.140 --> 00:00:17.140
I don't think learning has a purpose.

00:00:17.140 --> 00:00:19.100
I think learning happens.

00:00:19.100 --> 00:00:20.440
So the purpose of learning?

00:00:25.950 --> 00:00:34.890
For me, I think at its very basis, it's about growing

00:00:34.890 --> 00:00:39.600
your level of self awareness so you know better who you are,

00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:44.600
so you know better how you do, and then can impact the world.

00:00:44.600 --> 00:00:49.370
But when you really learn, it is when you do it as an act of freedom.

00:00:49.370 --> 00:00:53.650
You need to be a responsible citizen, and to be a responsible citizen you

00:00:53.650 --> 00:00:59.030
need to have a firm grasp of the issues that are surrounding you.

00:00:59.030 --> 00:01:03.100
Whether it's what's going on in your community, what's going on the world,

00:01:03.100 --> 00:01:07.100
and a lot of these things might have some basis in science or art

00:01:07.100 --> 00:01:12.580
or literature, and you can learn about all these different areas

00:01:12.580 --> 00:01:14.150
from very different inputs.

00:01:14.150 --> 00:01:17.050
Good, powerful, meaningful learning occurs

00:01:17.050 --> 00:01:22.490
when the interests of the learner is matched with the capacity of a tutor.

00:01:22.490 --> 00:01:28.530
So the basic idea is you learn well what you're interested in learning.

00:01:28.530 --> 00:01:31.360
The purpose of learning is a very big question.

00:01:34.770 --> 00:01:40.930
One way in which I think about it is that--

00:01:40.930 --> 00:01:44.610
and I think it comes from my background as a biologist--

00:01:44.610 --> 00:01:48.270
one of the fundamental features of all living things

00:01:48.270 --> 00:01:50.990
is that you change over time, right?

00:01:50.990 --> 00:01:56.550
And to stay still to in chemical terms or biochemical terms,

00:01:56.550 --> 00:01:59.830
to reach equilibrium is to die.

00:01:59.830 --> 00:02:02.980
So living things are always in a process of change.

00:02:02.980 --> 00:02:05.150
They're always in a dynamic state.

00:02:05.150 --> 00:02:10.320
And ultimately, I think learning is almost the engine that

00:02:10.320 --> 00:02:12.640
allows us to continue to be dynamic.

00:02:12.640 --> 00:02:22.450
So I want to separate the question of learning from the question of how

00:02:22.450 --> 00:02:28.990
we as a society, as a culture, as institutions,

00:02:28.990 --> 00:02:35.770
define both the kind of learning that matters, the kind of learning that we

00:02:35.770 --> 00:02:39.680
should measure, the kind of learning that becomes

00:02:39.680 --> 00:02:45.740
a threshold for other things, and the kind of learning that

00:02:45.740 --> 00:02:51.200
gives you a reward within the context of the institution.

00:02:51.200 --> 00:02:53.750
You need communication skills.

00:02:53.750 --> 00:02:56.400
You need reasoning skills.

00:02:56.400 --> 00:03:04.220
You need to develop your creative skills, and at Fenway High,

00:03:04.220 --> 00:03:13.200
specifically, learning is about getting that academic foundation that's

00:03:13.200 --> 00:03:19.800
going to prepare you to move on to post-secondary learning.

00:03:19.800 --> 00:03:25.720
But it's also developing a world perspective.

00:03:25.720 --> 00:03:27.920
So quite often when we think about learning,

00:03:27.920 --> 00:03:32.260
and if we think about learning in the digital environment,

00:03:32.260 --> 00:03:36.520
the temptation is to think that learning is a single sort of definition.

00:03:36.520 --> 00:03:39.820
But ultimately, from one field to another field,

00:03:39.820 --> 00:03:43.790
broadly speaking, the aspiration for learning can be quite different.

00:03:43.790 --> 00:03:49.220
I think the best way, the most efficient way,

00:03:49.220 --> 00:03:52.100
and the most powerful way to sort of decide what should be learned

00:03:52.100 --> 00:03:54.680
is to ask learners.

